# JSDoc documentation (required)

Every **exported** React component, function, custom hook, and meaningful non-trivial helper in `src/` must have a JSDoc block that explains purpose and documents props/parameters. Do this when creating or editing the symbol — do not leave new code undocumented.

## What to document

| Kind | Required |
|------|----------|
| React components (default or named export) | Summary + `@param props` (or each prop) |
| Custom hooks (`use*`) | Summary + each parameter + `@returns` |
| Exported functions / utilities | Summary + each `@param` + `@returns` when not `void` |
| Props / options types | Brief type-level comment when the shape is non-obvious |

**Skip only:** one-line pure helpers that are self-explanatory from the name (e.g. `cn`, tiny predicates), generated files, and re-export barrels (`index.ts`).

## Format

Use JSDoc (`/** ... */`), not `//` for public API. Prefer `@param` / `@returns` over repeating TypeScript types — describe *intent*, constraints, and side effects.

### Component

```tsx
type CourseCardProps = {
  /** Course title shown on the card */
  title: string;
  /** Destination for “Course Details” */
  href: string;
};

/**
 * Editorial course card with image overlay, meta table, and CTA.
 *
 * @param props - Card content and link target
 */
export default function CourseCard({ title, href }: CourseCardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

### Hook

```ts
/**
 * Tracks which faculty profile is most visible and drives TOC highlighting.
 *
 * @param teachers - Ordered faculty list used for scroll-spy ids
 * @returns Active teacher slug and a scroll-to-profile helper
 */
function useFacultyScrollSpy(teachers: TeacherProfile[]) {
  // ...
}
```

### Function

```ts
/**
 * Builds a WhatsApp enquire URL for an online course.
 *
 * @param courseTitle - Course name embedded in the prefilled message
 * @returns Absolute `wa.me` URL
 */
export function onlineEnquireHref(courseTitle: string): string {
  // ...
}
```

## Agent checklist

When adding or changing code in `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}`:

1. Add or update the JSDoc on every new/changed exported component, hook, and function.
2. Document props (inline on the props type fields and/or `@param props`).
3. Mention important side effects (scroll lock, DOM measurement, network, localStorage).
4. Do not invent unrelated refactors — document what you touch.
5. Keep comments accurate; if behavior changes, update the JSDoc in the same edit.
